+/* Block chaining. Generated code may stay inside its chunk across a loop
+ * back-edge, a bl, or a blr/bctr whose target is in the same chunk, instead of
+ * returning to the host's dispatch loop each time. It only does so when the
+ * host has published a stop table: one byte per word from
+ * dolrecomp_chain_stop_base, non-zero where the host must see the call (an
+ * HLE intercept or notify hook). Targets outside the table never chain. NULL
+ * (the default) keeps every branch going through the dispatch loop. */
